1
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:07,591
( knocking )

2
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:12,972
HEY.

3
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:21,689
MONICA?

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,941
WHAT TIME IS IT?

5
00:00:23,983 --> 00:00:27,486
AH, 9:00.

6
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:29,446
BUT IT'S DARK OUT.

7
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:34,201
WELL, THAT'S BECAUSE
YOU ALWAYS SLEEP
TILL NOON, SILLY.

8
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:36,787
THIS IS WHAT
9:00 LOOKS LIKE.

9
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:39,039
I GUESS I'LL GET WASHED UP THEN.

10
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:42,626
WATCH THAT SUN RISE.

11
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:48,173
I'M REALLY GETTING TIRED OF
SNEAKING AROUND ALL THE TIME.

12
00:00:48,215 --> 00:00:49,591
I KNOW. ME TOO.

13
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:51,677
HEY, WHAT IF WE WENT AWAY
FOR THE WHOLE WEEKEND?

14
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:53,178
YOU KNOW, HAD NO INTERRUPTIONS.

15
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,930
AND WE COULD BE NAKED
THE ENTIRE TIME.

16
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:56,015
ALL WEEKEND?

17
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,517
THAT'S A WHOLE LOT OF NAKED.

18
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:00,895
YEAH, I COULD SAY
THAT I HAVE A CONFERENCE

19
00:01:00,936 --> 00:01:03,104
AND YOU CAN SAY
YOU HAVE A CHEF THING.

20
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:05,190
OH, I'VE ALWAYS WANTED
TO GO TO THIS CULINARY FAIR

21
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:06,316
THAT THEY HAVE IN JERSEY.

22
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:08,569
OKAY, YOU KNOW
YOU'RE NOT, THOUGH.

23
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:10,696
LET'S GO.

24
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:13,782
WAIT, WHAT ABOUT JOEY?

25
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:31,299
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

26
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,677
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

27
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:36,555
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

28
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:41,018
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

29
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:42,978
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

30
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:46,023
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

31
00:01:46,065 --> 00:01:49,651
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

32
00:01:49,693 --> 00:01:51,737
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

33
00:01:51,779 --> 00:01:54,364
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

34
00:01:54,406 --> 00:01:56,575
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

35
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:59,787
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:05,417
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

37
00:02:08,127 --> 00:02:09,463
GUESS WHAT I'M DOING
THIS WEEKEND?

38
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:10,672
THIS CULINARY FAIR
IN JERSEY.

39
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,716
HOW WEIRD.

40
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:15,385
CHANDLER JUST TOLD US
HE'S GOT A CONFERENCE THERE.

41
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,262
OH, WELL, THAT'S FUNNY.

42
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,015
SEEMS LIKE CHANDLER'S CONFERENCE

43
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:23,518
COULD HAVE BEEN
IN CONNECTICUT OR VERMONT.

44
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:27,522
I'M NOT IN CHARGE OF WHERE
THE CONFERENCE IS HELD.

45
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:31,568
DO YOU WANT PEOPLE TO THINK
IT'S A FAKE CONFERENCE?

46
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,487
IT'S A REAL CONFERENCE.

47
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:37,324
HEY. IS RACHEL HERE?
I'VE GOT TO TALK TO HER.

48
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:38,408
NO, SHE'S OUT SHOPPING.

49
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:40,201
DAMN.

50
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,203
WHAT'S GOING ON?

51
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,872
I TOLD EMILY TO COME

52
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:48,209
AND I JUST NEED TO, YOU KNOW,
TALK TO RACHEL ABOUT IT.

53
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:49,419
WAIT A MINUTE.

54
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:51,170
SO, WHEN EMILY COMES

55
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:54,424
YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO SEE RACHEL ANYMORE?

56
00:02:54,466 --> 00:02:56,135
WELL, LOOK.
I'M JUST TRYING TO FOCUS

57
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,428
ON THE "I GET TO SEE MY WIFE"
PART, ALL RIGHT.

58
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,347
AND NOT THE PART
THAT MAKES ME DO THIS.

59
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,935
SO YOU GUYS ARE
NEVER GOING

60
00:03:04,977 --> 00:03:06,812
TO BE IN THE SAME
ROOM TOGETHER?

61
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:08,396
HOW IS THAT
GOING TO WORK?

62
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,815
I HAVE NO IDEA.

63
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:13,777
I MEAN, BUT I ASSURE YOU,
I WILL FIGURE IT OUT.

64
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:18,365
DOESN'T SEEM LIKE
IT'S GOING TO WORK.

65
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:20,993
HI, GUYS.

66
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:22,995
HI.
HEY.

67
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:24,454
WHAT'S GOING ON?

68
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:27,875
WE'RE FLIPPING
MONICA'S MATTRESS.

69
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:34,548
SO I'M THINKING BASICALLY, WE
PICK IT UP AND THEN WE FLIP IT.

70
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:38,218
THAT'S BETTER
THAN MY WAY.

71
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:42,514
OH, OKAY. HEY, GUYS.
WOULD YOU FLIP MINE TOO?

72
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:45,350
( all groaning )

73
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:50,189
OH, LOOK.
A LETTER FROM MY MOM.

74
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:54,568
SO, RACH...

75
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,987
YOU KNOW HOW EMILY
IS COMING, RIGHT?

76
00:03:57,029 --> 00:03:58,822
OH, YEAH. I KNOW.

77
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,699
CAN YOU HEAR ANYTHING?

78
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:03,077
OH, YES. SOMEBODY JUST SAID,
"CAN YOU HEAR ANYTHING?"

79
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:11,043
HEY, JOEY'S ASS.

80
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,629
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

81
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,715
WELL, REMEMBER WHEN THEY GOT
INTO THAT BIG FIGHT

82
00:04:16,757 --> 00:04:19,134
AND BROKE UP AND WE WERE ALL
STUCK IN HERE ALL NIGHT

83
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:20,552
WITH NO FOOD OR ANYTHING?

84
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:22,930
WELL, WHEN ROSS SAID
RACHEL AT THE WEDDING

85
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:25,807
I FIGURE IT WAS GOING
TO HAPPEN AGAIN, YOU KNOW.

86
00:04:25,849 --> 00:04:27,184
SO I HID THIS IN HERE.

87
00:04:27,226 --> 00:04:29,644
OOH. CANDY BARS,
CROSSWORD PUZZLES.

88
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:33,440
OOH, MAD LIBS, MINE.

89
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,316
CONDOMS?

90
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:41,115
HEY, YOU DON'T KNOW HOW LONG
WE'RE GOING TO BE IN HERE.

91
00:04:41,156 --> 00:04:43,324
WE MAY HAVE TO REPOPULATE
THE EARTH.

92
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:47,788
AND CONDOMS ARE THE WAY
TO DO THAT?

93
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:54,128
ANYWAY, IT ALL
BOILS DOWN TO THIS.

94
00:04:54,169 --> 00:04:56,004
THE LAST TIME
I TALKED TO EMILY...

95
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:58,924
OH, MY GOD! OUR DOG DIED.

96
00:04:58,966 --> 00:05:01,135
WHAT?

97
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:04,596
OH, MY GOD.
LAPOOH, OUR DOG.

98
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:07,682
LAPOOH'S STILL ALIVE?

99
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:12,771
OH, IT SAYS HE WAS HIT
BY AN ICE CREAM TRUCK.

100
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:16,858
AND DRAGGED
FOR NINE... TEEN BLOCKS.

101
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:17,943
OH, MY GOD.

102
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:21,155
SWEETIE, WE HEARD YOU CRYING.

103
00:05:21,196 --> 00:05:22,697
PLEASE DON'T CRY.

104
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,241
IT'S LAPOOH.

105
00:05:24,283 --> 00:05:26,785
I KNOW, IT'S LAPOOH RIGHT NOW,
BUT IT WILL GET BETTER.

106
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,544
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.
WE'RE HERE.

107
00:05:38,672 --> 00:05:40,757
OOH, CHOCOLATES ON THE PILLOWS.
OH, I LOVE THAT.

108
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:43,844
OH, YOU SHOULD LIVE WITH JOEY.
ROLLOS EVERYWHERE.

109
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,181
OKAY, I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

110
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:55,480
OH, YES.

111
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,607
GET IN HERE. THERE'S
A HIGH-SPEED CAR CHASE ON.

112
00:05:57,649 --> 00:06:00,652
WE'RE SWITCHING ROOMS.

113
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:02,779
OH, DEAR GOD.
THEY GAVE US GLASSES.

114
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:05,157
NO, THEY GAVE US GLASSES
WITH LIPSTICK ON THEM.

115
00:06:05,199 --> 00:06:07,326
I MEAN... IF THEY
DIDN'T CHANGE THE GLASSES

116
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,368
WHO KNOWS WHAT ELSE
THEY DIDN'T CHANGE.

117
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:11,955
OH, COME ON, SWEETIE.

118
00:06:11,997 --> 00:06:14,582
I JUST WANT THIS WEEKEND
TO BE PERFECT, OKAY.

119
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:17,002
WE CAN CHANGE ROOMS, CAN'T WE?

120
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:18,337
OKAY, BUT LET'S DO IT NOW

121
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:20,379
BECAUSE CHOPPER 5
JUST LOST ITS FEED.

122
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:29,014
HEY, SO, AH, YOU KNOW
HOW THERE WAS SOMETHING

123
00:06:29,056 --> 00:06:31,266
I WANTED TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT?

124
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:33,143
OH, YEAH.

125
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:38,773
WELL, YOU KNOW HOW I'M TRYING
TO WORK THINGS OUT WITH EMILY?

126
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:43,778
WELL, THERE'S THIS ONE THING.

127
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,864
OKAY...

128
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:47,908
HERE GOES.

129
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:52,954
I MADE A PROMISE THAT...

130
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:54,039
OH, HEY.

131
00:06:54,081 --> 00:06:55,082
WHAT?

132
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,875
YOUR NOSE IS BLEEDING.
OH, GOD.

133
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,586
OH, NOT AGAIN.

134
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:01,462
THIS HAPPENED
WHEN MY GRANDFATHER DIED.

135
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,421
IT'S...

136
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,965
I'M SORRY.

137
00:07:04,007 --> 00:07:05,800
OH, GROSS.

138
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:09,470
OKAY, SO I'M SORRY.
WHAT DID YOU WANT TO TELL ME?

139
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,226
UH...

140
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:17,229
( snorts )

141
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:19,022
SORRY.

142
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:20,648
I, UH...

143
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:25,570
I CAN'T SEE YOU ANYMORE.

144
00:07:25,612 --> 00:07:27,989
I KNOW, IT'S RIDICULOUS.

145
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:30,367
I CAN'T SEE YOU EITHER.

146
00:07:30,409 --> 00:07:33,995
I THINK YOU'LL FIND THIS ROOM
MORE TO YOUR LIKING.

147
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,538
OKAY, GREAT.

148
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,795
THEY SAY HE'S ONLY GOT
HALF A TANK LEFT.

149
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:46,425
HALF A TANK. WE STILL GOT A LOT
OF HIGH-SPEED CHASING TO DO.

150
00:07:46,465 --> 00:07:48,135
WE'RE SWITCHING ROOMS AGAIN.

151
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:49,844
WHAT? WHY?

152
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:53,598
THIS IS A GARDEN VIEW ROOM AND
WE PAID FOR AN OCEAN VIEW ROOM.

153
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:59,062
OUR LAST OCEAN VIEW ROOM
WAS UNACCEPTABLE TO YOU.

154
00:07:59,104 --> 00:08:00,688
EXCUSE ME.

155
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,899
UM, CAN I TALK TO YOU
OVER HERE FOR JUST A SECOND?

156
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:03,984
UH-HUH.

157
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,113
CHANDLER?

158
00:08:08,155 --> 00:08:09,114
YEAH.

159
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:10,489
OKAY, LOOK.

160
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,659
THESE CLOWNS ARE TRYING
TO TAKE US FOR A RIDE

161
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,119
AND I'M NOT GOING TO LET THEM.

162
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:15,829
NOW, WE'RE NOT
A COUPLE OF SUCKERS.

163
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:18,248
I HEAR YA, MUGSY.

164
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,751
BUT LOOK, ALL THESE ROOMS
ARE FINE, OKAY.

165
00:08:21,793 --> 00:08:24,587
CAN YOU JUST PICK ONE
SO I CAN WATCH THE...

166
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:28,508
HAVE A PERFECT MAGICAL WEEKEND
TOGETHER WITH YOU?

167
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:33,680
OKAY, THIS ONE I LIKE.

168
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:34,431
NOTHING.

169
00:08:34,473 --> 00:08:35,932
NOTHING, IT'S OVER.

170
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:39,769
DAMN IT. THIS IS REGULARLY
SCHEDULED PROGRAMMING.

171
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:41,355
CAN WE TURN THE TV OFF?

172
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:45,317
DO WE REALLY WANT TO SPEND
THE ENTIRE WEEKEND LIKE THIS?

173
00:08:45,359 --> 00:08:47,194
OH, I'M SORRY. AM I
GETTING IN THE WAY

174
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,695
OF ALL THE
ROOM-SWITCHING FUN?

175
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:51,490
DON'T BLAME ME
FOR RUINING TONIGHT.

176
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,740
WHO SHOULD I BLAME?

177
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,034
THE NICE BELLMAN
WHO DRAGGED OUR LUGGAGE

178
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:54,868
TO TEN DIFFERENT ROOMS?

179
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,286
HOW ABOUT THE IDIOT

180
00:08:56,328 --> 00:08:58,372
WHO THOUGHT HE COULD DRIVE
FROM ALBANY TO CANADA

181
00:08:58,413 --> 00:08:59,456
ON HALF A TANK OF GAS?

182
00:08:59,498 --> 00:09:04,002
DO NOT SPEAK ILL
OF THE DEAD.

183
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:08,756
WE'RE SUPPOSED TO BE SPENDING
A ROMANTIC WEEKEND TOGETHER.

184
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,176
WHAT'S THE MATTER WITH YOU?

185
00:09:11,218 --> 00:09:13,636
I JUST WANT TO WATCH
A LITTLE TELEVISION.

186
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,929
WHAT IS THE BIG DEAL?

187
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,014
GEEZ, RELAX, MOM.

188
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:20,185
WHAT DID YOU SAY?

189
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:24,147
I SAID, GEEZ,
RELAX, MONNN.

190
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,199
HEY.

191
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:35,450
WHAT'S UP?

192
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,993
RACHEL, I'VE BEEN WANTING

193
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:39,246
TO TELL YOU SOMETHING
FOR A WHILE NOW

194
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,748
AND I REALLY...
I JUST HAVE TO GET IT OUT.

195
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:43,542
OKAY, ALL RIGHT. WHAT'S UP?

196
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,668
OKAY...

197
00:09:47,421 --> 00:09:49,005
YOU KNOW HOW YOU TOLD ME

198
00:09:49,047 --> 00:09:52,342
I SHOULD DO WHATEVER IT TAKES
TO FIX MY MARRIAGE?

199
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:55,762
YEAH. I TOLD YOU TO GIVE EMILY
WHATEVER SHE WANTS.

200
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:59,349
AND WHILE THAT WAS GOOD ADVICE

201
00:09:59,391 --> 00:10:03,853
YOU SHOULD KNOW THAT
WHAT SHE WANTS...

202
00:10:03,895 --> 00:10:05,146
YEAH?

203
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:09,776
IS FOR ME NOT
TO SEE YOU ANYMORE.

204
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:13,530
WELL, THAT'S CRAZY.
YOU CAN'T DO THAT.

205
00:10:13,572 --> 00:10:16,783
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO TELL HER?

206
00:10:20,287 --> 00:10:24,999
OH, MY GOD.

207
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:27,377
YOU'VE ALREADY AGREED TO THIS,
HAVEN'T YOU?

208
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:28,711
IT'S AWFUL, I KNOW.

209
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,713
I... I MEAN, I FEEL TERRIBLE

210
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:34,342
BUT I HAVE TO DO THIS
IF I WANT MY MARRIAGE TO WORK.

211
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:35,635
AND I DO.

212
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:38,179
I HAVE TO MAKE
THIS MARRIAGE WORK.

213
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:39,431
I HAVE TO.

214
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,311
BUT THE GOOD THING IS

215
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:47,230
WE CAN STILL SEE EACH OTHER
UNTIL SHE GETS HERE.

216
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,984
OH!

217
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,320
OH, LUCKY ME!

218
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:55,447
OH, MY GOD,
THAT IS GOOD NEWS, ROSS.

219
00:10:55,489 --> 00:10:57,365
I THINK
THAT'S THE BEST NEWS

220
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,159
I'VE HEARD SINCE LAPOOH DIED.

221
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:05,039
YOU HAVE NO IDEA
WHAT A NIGHTMARE THIS HAS BEEN.

222
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:07,041
THIS IS SO HARD.

223
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,835
OH, YEAH, REALLY.
IS IT, ROSS?

224
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:10,337
YEAH, OKAY.

225
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,713
WELL, LET ME JUST MAKE THIS
A LITTLE EASIER FOR YOU.

226
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,466
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?
STORMING OUT.

227
00:11:14,508 --> 00:11:16,009
RACHEL, THIS IS YOUR APARTMENT.

228
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:19,012
YEAH, WELL,
THAT'S HOW MAD I AM.

229
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:34,569
DAMN ROLLOS!

230
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:36,946
HEY, YOU'RE BACK.
HEY.

231
00:11:36,988 --> 00:11:39,366
HOW WAS YOUR CONFERENCE?

232
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:40,783
IT WAS TERRIBLE.

233
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:43,203
I FOUGHT WITH MY COLLEAGUES
THE ENTIRE TIME.

234
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,996
ARE YOU KIDDING WITH THIS?

235
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:46,122
( candy clatters )

236
00:11:46,164 --> 00:11:48,833
SO YOUR WEEKEND
WAS A TOTAL BUST?

237
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:51,419
UH, NO. I SAW DONALD TRUMP
WAITING FOR AN ELEVATOR.

238
00:11:51,461 --> 00:11:52,671
OH.

239
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:54,713
HI.

240
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:56,341
HEY, YOU'RE BACK, TOO.

241
00:11:56,383 --> 00:11:58,009
YEAH. CHANDLER,
CAN I TALK TO YOU

242
00:11:58,051 --> 00:11:59,010
FOR JUST A SECOND?

243
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,303
HOW WAS YOUR CHEF THING?

244
00:12:00,345 --> 00:12:01,888
IT WAS AWFUL.

245
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:05,099
GUESS SOME PEOPLE JUST DON'T
APPRECIATE REALLY GOOD FOOD.

246
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,143
WELL, MAYBE IT WAS
THE KIND OF FOOD

247
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:08,645
THAT TASTED GOOD AT FIRST

248
00:12:08,687 --> 00:12:11,690
BUT THEN MADE EVERYBODY VOMIT
AND HAVE DIARRHEA.

249
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:14,192
CHANDLER?

250
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:16,403
MONICA?

251
00:12:17,571 --> 00:12:20,156
OKAY. I'D LIKE TO KNOW
HOW MUCH THE ROOM WAS

252
00:12:20,198 --> 00:12:21,866
'CAUSE I WANT
TO PAY MY HALF.

253
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:23,159
OKAY, FINE. $300.

254
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:24,369
$300?

255
00:12:24,411 --> 00:12:26,705
YEAH. JUST THINK OF IT
AS $25 PER ROOM.

256
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:30,667
( groans )

257
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:33,002
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS
WOOFING ABOUT?

258
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:35,213
CHANDLER STOLE A 20
FROM MY PURSE.

259
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:37,048
NO!

260
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:40,552
YOU KNOW WHAT?

261
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:42,345
NOW THAT I THINK ABOUT IT

262
00:12:42,387 --> 00:12:44,889
I CONSTANTLY FIND
MYSELF WITHOUT 20s

263
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:48,017
AND YOU ALWAYS HAVE LOTS.

264
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,525
YOU SHOULD HAVE SEEN
THE LOOK ON HER FACE.

265
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:57,611
I DON'T WANT RACHEL
TO HATE ME.

266
00:12:57,652 --> 00:12:59,237
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO DO.

267
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:00,405
DO YOU WANT MY ADVICE?

268
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:01,573
YES, PLEASE.

269
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:02,781
YOU WON'T LIKE IT.

270
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,743
THAT'S OKAY.

271
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:08,204
YOU GOT MARRIED TOO FAST.

272
00:13:08,246 --> 00:13:10,290
THAT'S NOT ADVICE.

273
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:11,583
I TOLD YOU.

274
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:15,794
I'M GOING TO THE BATHROOM.

275
00:13:18,298 --> 00:13:21,175
MAN, IF ANYONE ASKED ME
TO GIVE UP ANY OF YOU

276
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,927
I DON'T THINK
I COULD DO IT.

277
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:23,928
ME, NEITHER.

278
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,888
MAYBE I COULD DO IT.

279
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:30,685
HI.
HI, RACH.

280
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:33,062
LOOK, I KNOW YOU GUYS
HEARD ABOUT THE WHOLE THING

281
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,522
WITH ME AND ROSS

282
00:13:34,564 --> 00:13:36,608
BUT, YOU KNOW, I'VE BEEN
OBSESSING ABOUT IT ALL DAY

283
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:39,068
AND I WOULD JUST LOVE
NOT TO TALK ABOUT IT, ALL
RIGHT?

284
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:42,405
UH, I DON'T KNOW IF THIS
FALLS UNDER THAT CATEGORY

285
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:44,699
BUT, UH, ROSS IS
RIGHT BACK THERE.

286
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:46,284
THAT'S NOT ROSS.

287
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:47,619
OH, NO. NOT THAT GUY.

288
00:13:47,661 --> 00:13:49,621
HE DOES LOOK LIKE HIM, THOUGH.

289
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,957
OKAY. ROSS IS IN THE BATHROOM.

290
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:53,958
OH, MY GOD.

291
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,042
IT'S HAPPENING.

292
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:56,127
IT'S ALREADY STARTED.

293
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:57,128
I'M KIP.

294
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,547
YOU'RE NOT KIP.

295
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,257
DO YOU EVEN KNOW WHO KIP IS?

296
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:02,967
WHO CARES?

297
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:05,386
YOU'RE RACHEL.

298
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:08,431
WHO'S KIP?

299
00:14:08,473 --> 00:14:09,724
KIP, MY OLD ROOMMATE.

300
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:12,059
WE ALL USED TO
HANG OUT TOGETHER?

301
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:14,813
OH, THAT POOR BASTARD.

302
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,230
SEE? YOU TOLD ME THE STORY.

303
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,315
HE AND MONICA DATED.

304
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:18,733
WHEN THEY BROKE UP

305
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:21,152
THEY COULDN'T EVEN BE
IN THE SAME ROOM TOGETHER

306
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:23,404
AND YOU ALL PROMISED
YOU WOULD STAY HIS FRIEND

307
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:24,656
AND WHAT HAPPENED?

308
00:14:24,698 --> 00:14:25,824
HE GOT PHASED OUT.

309
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,534
YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO BE PHASED OUT.

310
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:28,785
WELL, OF COURSE, I AM.

311
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:30,662
IT'S NOT GOING
TO HAPPEN TO ROSS.

312
00:14:30,704 --> 00:14:31,746
HE'S YOUR BROTHER.

313
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:33,373
HE'S YOUR OLD
COLLEGE ROOMMATE.

314
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,582
IT'S JUST A MATTER OF TIME

315
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:36,334
BEFORE SOMEONE HAD
TO LEAVE THE GROUP.

316
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:37,960
I ALWAYS ASSUMED
IT WOULD BE PHOEBE.

317
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:39,170
UH!

318
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,842
COME ON. YOU LIVE FAR AWAY,
YOU'RE NOT RELATED

319
00:14:43,882 --> 00:14:45,176
YOU LIFT RIGHT OUT.

320
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:52,559
HEY.

321
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,892
HEY, MR. BING.

322
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:59,190
THAT HOTEL
YOU STAYED AT CALLED.

323
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:02,276
SAID SOMEONE LEFT
AN EYELASH CURLER IN YOUR ROOM.

324
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:08,199
YES, THAT WAS MINE.

325
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:09,617
'CAUSE I FIGURED

326
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:11,160
YOU HOOKED UP WITH SOME GIRL
AND SHE LEFT IT.

327
00:15:11,202 --> 00:15:14,038
YES, THAT WOULD HAVE
MADE MORE SENSE.

328
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:18,084
YOU KNOW, I DON'T EVEN FEEL
LIKE I KNOW YOU ANYMORE, MAN.

329
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:21,170
ALL RIGHT? LOOK

330
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:24,257
I'M JUST GOING TO ASK YOU THIS
ONE TIME, ALL RIGHT?

331
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:25,925
WHATEVER YOU SAY,
I'LL BELIEVE YOU.

332
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:31,097
WERE YOU OR WERE YOU NOT
ON A GAY CRUISE?

333
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:46,487
PHOEBE?

334
00:15:48,907 --> 00:15:53,119
I'M SORRY ABOUT THE WHOLE
LIFTING-OUT THING.

335
00:15:54,621 --> 00:15:57,081
LOOK, YOU GOT
TO COME WITH ME.

336
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:57,874
COME WHERE?

337
00:15:57,916 --> 00:15:58,875
WHEREVER I GO.

338
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:00,042
COME ON.

339
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,462
YOU AND ME--
WE'LL START A NEW GROUP.

340
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:04,130
WE'RE THE BEST ONES.

341
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:09,636
OKAY, BUT TRY
TO GET JOEY, TOO.

342
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:13,139
PHEEBS, DO YOU MIND

343
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,767
IF I SPEAK TO RACHEL
ALONE FOR A SEC?

344
00:16:15,809 --> 00:16:17,936
OH, SURE. YEAH.

345
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:21,940
BYE, ROSS...

346
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,566
( whispers ):
FOREVER.

347
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,279
HI.

348
00:16:28,321 --> 00:16:30,406
HI. WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

349
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:32,659
ISN'T THIS AGAINST THE RULES?

350
00:16:34,993 --> 00:16:36,496
I TALKED TO MONICA.

351
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:42,168
LOOK, I'M THE ONE
WHO MADE THE CHOICE.

352
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:44,921
I'M THE ONE WHO'S
MAKING THINGS CHANGE

353
00:16:44,963 --> 00:16:48,382
SO I SHOULD BE THE ONE
TO, YOU KNOW, STEP BACK.

354
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:49,383
OH, ROSS...

355
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,636
NO. NO, IT'S
OKAY, REALLY.

356
00:16:51,678 --> 00:16:53,304
THERE ARE PLENTY OF PEOPLE

357
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:56,015
WHO JUST SEE THEIR SISTERS
AT THANKSGIVING

358
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:59,059
AND JUST SEE THEIR COLLEGE
ROOMMATES AT REUNIONS

359
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:01,896
AND JUST SEE JOEY
AT BURGER KING.

360
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:07,944
SO, IS THAT BETTER?

361
00:17:11,531 --> 00:17:13,825
NO, IT'S NOT BETTER.

362
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:17,077
I STILL DON'T GET
TO SEE YOU.

363
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,998
WELL, WHAT WOULD
YOU DO, RACH?

364
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:23,334
IF YOU WERE ME,
WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

365
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:32,635
WELL, FOR STARTERS

366
00:17:32,677 --> 00:17:35,179
I WOULD HAVE SAID
THE RIGHT NAME
AT MY WEDDING.

367
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:44,188
I CAN'T BELIEVE
THIS IS HAPPENING.

368
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,652
I KNOW.

369
00:17:49,694 --> 00:17:52,947
I AM SO SORRY.

370
00:17:52,989 --> 00:17:56,367
I KNOW THAT, TOO.

371
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:04,417
( clears throat )

372
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:05,585
HEY, RACH?

373
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:07,378
SORRY TO INTERRUPT,
BUT PHOEBE SAID

374
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:10,089
YOU WANT TO TALK TO ME
ABOUT A TRIP OR SOMETHING.

375
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,220
HEY.

376
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,765
HI.

377
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:23,561
I JUST CAME OVER
TO DROP OFF... NOTHING.

378
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:29,149
SO, THAT WEEKEND
KIND OF SUCKED, HUH?

379
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:31,151
YEAH, IT DID.

380
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:33,905
SO I GUESS THIS IS OVER.

381
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:35,907
WHAT?

382
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:37,992
WELL, YOU KNOW, YOU AND ME.

383
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:39,786
IT HAD TO END SOMETIME.

384
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,288
WHY, EXACTLY?

385
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,831
BECAUSE OF THE WEEKEND.

386
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:44,874
WE HAD A FIGHT.

387
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,709
CHANDLER, THAT'S CRAZY.

388
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:48,586
IF YOU GIVE UP
EVERY TIME

389
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:50,880
YOU HAVE A FIGHT
WITH SOMEONE

390
00:18:50,922 --> 00:18:54,092
YOU'D NEVER BE WITH
ANYONE LONGER THAN...

391
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:58,429
OH!

392
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:02,558
SO, THIS ISN'T OVER?

393
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:06,604
YOU ARE SO CUTE.

394
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:10,066
NO, NO.

395
00:19:10,108 --> 00:19:11,734
IT WAS A FIGHT.

396
00:19:11,776 --> 00:19:13,987
YOU DEAL WITH IT
AND YOU MOVE ON.

397
00:19:14,028 --> 00:19:16,238
IT'S NOTHING
TO FREAK OUT ABOUT.

398
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,616
REALLY? OKAY. GREAT.

399
00:19:18,658 --> 00:19:19,742
AW...

400
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:23,079
WELCOME TO AN ADULT
RELATIONSHIP.

401
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,334
WE'RE IN A RELATIONSHIP?

402
00:19:31,129 --> 00:19:33,047
I'M AFRAID SO.

403
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,548
OKAY.

404
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:40,763
HEY.

405
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:41,764
HEY.

406
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:42,765
OH, HEY, MONICA.

407
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,391
I HEARD YOU SAW
DONALD TRUMP

408
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,601
AT YOUR CONVENTION.

409
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:47,478
YEAH. SAW HIM WAITING
FOR AN ELEVATOR.

410
00:19:49,689 --> 00:19:51,315
Monica:
HEY, RACH,
CAN I BORROW

411
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:52,984
YOUR EYELASH CURLER?
I LOST MINE.

412
00:19:53,026 --> 00:19:54,152
IT'S IN THE BATHROOM.

413
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:00,700
OH!

414
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:04,244
JOEY, CAN I TALK
TO YOU FOR A SECOND?

415
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,329
OOH! OH!

416
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:06,998
I NEED TO TALK
TO YOU RIGHT NOW.

417
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:09,125
OH! OH! OH!

418
00:20:10,877 --> 00:20:12,628
OH...!

419
00:20:17,091 --> 00:20:19,093
YES.

420
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:21,554
YES.

421
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:24,849
YOU AND, AND YOU?

422
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:27,351
YES, BUT YOU CANNOT
TELL ANYONE.

423
00:20:27,393 --> 00:20:28,394
NO ONE KNOWS.

424
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,437
HOW? WHEN?

425
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,106
IT HAPPENED IN LONDON.

426
00:20:32,148 --> 00:20:33,273
IN LONDON!

427
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:37,319
THE REASON
WE DIDN'T TELL ANYONE

428
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,780
WAS 'CAUSE WE DIDN'T WANT
TO MAKE A BIG DEAL OUT OF IT.

429
00:20:39,822 --> 00:20:41,615
BUT IT IS A BIG DEAL.

430
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,659
I HAVE TO TELL SOMEONE!

431
00:20:43,701 --> 00:20:46,913
YOU CAN'T.

432
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:48,748
PLEASE, PLEASE.
WE JUST DON'T WANT

433
00:20:48,789 --> 00:20:50,666
TO DEAL WITH TELLING
EVERYONE, OKAY?

434
00:20:50,708 --> 00:20:52,251
JUST PROMISE
YOU WON'T TELL.

435
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:59,133
ALL RIGHT!

436
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:01,427
MAN, THIS IS UNBELIEVABLE.

437
00:21:01,468 --> 00:21:03,554
I MEAN, IT'S GREAT!

438
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:04,597
BUT...

439
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,807
I KNOW, IT'S GREAT.

440
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:11,020
I DON'T WANT
TO SEE THAT.

441
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:16,192
WE'RE SO STUPID.

442
00:21:16,234 --> 00:21:18,194
DO YOU KNOW WHAT'S
GOING ON IN THERE?

443
00:21:18,236 --> 00:21:19,779
THEY'RE TRYING TO TAKE JOEY.

444
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:29,455
"THE POPULAR PHOEBE IN TENNIS
IS THE 'OVERHAND PHOEBE'

445
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:31,331
"AND IF YOU WIN, YOU MUST SLAP

446
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:34,585
YOUR OPPONENT ON THE PHOEBE
AND SAY, 'MY PHOEBE.'"

447
00:21:36,294 --> 00:21:37,838
THAT'S CUTE.

448
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:40,091
WE REALLY ALL ENJOYED IT,
BUT YOU KNOW IT DOESN'T COUNT.

449
00:21:40,133 --> 00:21:41,383
COUNT FOR WHAT?

450
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:45,387
JUST COUNT IN OUR HEADS
AS GOOD MAD LIBS.

451
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,473
I'M DONE.
IT'S OVER.

452
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:51,060
NO, WAIT. WAIT, GUYS,
IF WE FOLLOW THE RULES

453
00:21:51,102 --> 00:21:53,562
IT'S STILL FUN
AND IT MEANS SOMETHING.

454
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:55,815
I'M GOING
TO TAKE OFF.

455
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,108
GUYS, RULES ARE GOOD.

456
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:59,777
RULES HELP CONTROL THE FUN.

457
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:06,951
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

